# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Two purposes:
#   1. Catch bare-directory landings that would otherwise 404 (e.g., a user
#      typing "archstandard.org/standard/" from intuition).
#   2. Forward pre-/v1/-migration paths to their /v1/-prefixed equivalents.
#
# Order matters — first match wins. Specific rules go before wildcards.
#
# NOTE: /schema/* is intentionally NOT redirected. The JSON Schema's own $id
# is `https://archstandard.org/schema/v1.0.0/ads.schema.json` and the file
# is served at the dist root (per scripts/post-build.cjs ROOT_KEEP) so the
# canonical URL resolves directly. A wildcard redirect here would break
# the schema's self-referencing $id.

# 1. Renamed pages — preserve old bookmarks after a content rename.
/v1/standard/3-2-process-view/   /v1/standard/3-2-integration-view/   301
/standard/3-2-process-view/      /v1/standard/3-2-integration-view/   301

# 2. Bare-directory landings — intuitive guesses that would otherwise 404
#    because the directory contains assets, not an index.html.
/v1/standard/         /v1/standard/overview/        301
/v1/templates/        /v1/standard/templates/       301
/v1/cheat-cards/      /v1/guidance/cheat-cards/     301
/v1/prompts/          /v1/standard/prompts/         301
/v1/schema/           /v1/standard/schema/          301
/standard/            /v1/standard/overview/        301
/templates/           /v1/standard/templates/       301
/cheat-cards/         /v1/guidance/cheat-cards/     301
/prompts/             /v1/standard/prompts/         301

# 3. Pre-/v1/-migration: forward old sub-paths to /v1/-prefixed.
#    These match anything BELOW the listed paths (e.g. /standard/3-1-...)
#    and are placed after the specific bare-landing rules so they don't
#    shadow them.
/standard/*    /v1/standard/:splat    301
/examples/*    /v1/examples/:splat    301
/fr/*          /v1/fr/:splat          301
/de/*          /v1/de/:splat          301
/templates/*   /v1/templates/:splat   301
